  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Stakes**: Each player antes to the pool (or dealer antes four). 2. **Auction**: Eldest opens; players bid or pass in ascending order: Solo, Casco (with both black Aces), Dimidiator (exchange with called King), Alliance (call a King for partner). If all pass, Forced Spadille: holder of Spadille becomes Hombre and calls a King. 3. **Trump**: Hombre names trump (or partner may in Forced Spadille). 4. **Play**: Eldest leads. Must follow suit; may play any card if void. Highest trump wins, else highest of led suit. Spadille, Manille, Basta may be held back when trumps are led (unless a higher trump is led). 5. **Settlement**: Hombre wins or loses; pool and premiums paid accordingly.',
    Player: 'Four players bid for the right to be Hombre. Win the auction, name trump, and call a King to find a secret partnerâ€”or play Solo. Win six of ten tricks to take the pool. Watch out for Spadille, Manille, and Basta: the matadors that rule the trumps.',
    objective: 'As Hombre (declarer), win at least six of the ten tricks, either alone (Solo) or with a partner (Alliance). Opponents aim to prevent this.',
    gameplay: '1. **Stakes**: Each player antes to the pool (or dealer antes four). 2. **Auction**: Eldest opens; players bid or pass in ascending order: Solo, Casco (with both black Aces), Dimidiator (exchange with called King), Alliance (call a King for partner). If all pass, Forced Spadille: holder of Spadille becomes Hombre and calls a King. 3. **Trump**: Hombre names trump (or partner may in Forced Spadille). 4. **Play**: Eldest leads. Must follow suit; may play any card if void. Highest trump wins, else highest of led suit. Spadille, Manille, Basta may be held back when trumps are led (unless a higher trump is led). 5. **Settlement**: Hombre wins or loses; pool and premiums paid accordingly.',
    keyRules: [
      'Spadille (Ace of Spades) is always the highest trump.',
      'Basta (Ace of Clubs) is always the third highest trump.',
      'Manille = lowest card of trump suit (2 in black suits, 7 in red suits); always second highest trump.',
      'Red suits (plain): K > Q > J > A > 2 > 3 > 4 > 5 > 6 > 7. Black suits (plain): K > Q > J > 7 > 6 > 5 > 4 > 3 > 2.',
      'Alliance: Hombre calls a non-trump King; holder is secret partner until the called card is played.',
      'Forced Spadille: No vole; Hombre and partner aim for six tricks.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players. Each plays for herself; temporary alliances form per deal via the called King.',
      deck: '40 cards: A, K, Q, J, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 in each suit (8s, 9s, 10s removed).',
      equipment: '40-card pack, counters or chips for stakes, score sheet.',
      dealing: '1. Dealer shuffles; pone cuts. 2. Deal 10 cards each in batches of 4-3-3, 3-4-3, or 3-3-4. 3. Deal and play rotate right (counterclockwise).',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Stakes**: Each player antes to the pool (or dealer antes four). 2. **Auction**: Eldest opens; players bid or pass in ascending order: Solo, Casco (with both black Aces), Dimidiator (exchange with called King), Alliance (call a King for partner). If all pass, Forced Spadille: holder of Spadille becomes Hombre and calls a King. 3. **Trump**: Hombre names trump (or partner may in Forced Spadille). 4. **Play**: Eldest leads. Must follow suit; may play any card if void. Highest trump wins, else highest of led suit. Spadille, Manille, Basta may be held back when trumps are led (unless a higher trump is led). 5. **Settlement**: Hombre wins or loses; pool and premiums paid accordingly.',
